# ASSAY environment.
#
#   cp -n .env.example .env; chmod 600 .env
#
# -n, and never without it: copying this template over a working .env is how the key behind
# ERC-8004 identity 95265 was lost. Keys are written by `pnpm wallets` / `pnpm buyer`, which refuse
# to overwrite a value and keep dated copies in ~/.assay.
#
# NOTHING here is needed to run the sweeper, the verifier, the wall or the MCP server. Those are
# public chain reads against Robinhood Chain 4663 and work with an empty .env — which is the point
# of the architecture, not an accident of it. `pnpm sweep`, `pnpm test` and `pnpm mcp` all run as
# cloned.
#
# Each variable below says which commands need it. Every script that needs one validates it up
# front and exits with a message naming it, rather than failing somewhere in the middle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERV Reasoning — the adjudicator and the BRAID measurement harness.
# Needed by: pnpm ab, pnpm trials, pnpm hard, pnpm inject
# Get one at console.openserv.ai/settings/keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERV_API_KEY=serv_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenServ agent credentials, from .openserv.json after `pnpm provision`
# (agents.assay.apiKey and agents.assay.authToken).
# Needed by: pnpm serve:remote
#
# These are the ONLY secrets the production host holds. serve-remote.ts refuses to start if a
# signing key is also present, so a compromise of that box cannot reach funds or the identity NFT.
#
# .openserv.json itself is a secret file too, and the one this template cannot rebuild. Its
# userApiKey is the only credential for the OpenServ account that owns both paid workflows: that
# account was created by signing in with a wallet whose key is lost, and signing in with the
# current one reaches a different, empty account. Mode 600, gitignored, and copied to
# ~/.assay/openserv.json.backup.<time> by every script that lets provision() write it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENSERV_API_KEY=
OPENSERV_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wallet A — service owner. Owns the ERC-8004 identity NFT and receives every x402 payment.
# Needed by: pnpm mint, pnpm attest:submit, pnpm balances, pnpm provision, pnpm serve
# Written by `pnpm wallets`. `pnpm provision` refuses to run without it rather than let the
# vendor SDK mint one and write .env itself. Keep this and the ERC-8004 signer the SAME key, or a
# later setAgentURI reverts "Not authorized". Fund with ~0.001 ETH on Base 8453.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wallet B — buyer agent, so a settled payment has a genuinely distinct payer on-chain.
# Needed by: pnpm pay, pnpm balances
# Generated by `pnpm buyer`, which refuses to overwrite an existing value. Fund with ~$0.50 USDC
# on Base; it needs NO ETH, because x402 settles via an EIP-3009 signature and a relayer pays gas.
#
# `pnpm prove <payTo> [buyer]` needs only the buyer's public ADDRESS, as its second argument or
# BUYER_ADDRESS, so anyone can check a settlement without a key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUYER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# BUYER_ADDRESS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP server over SSE. Defaults shown; override in the systemd unit, not here.
# MCP_HOST defaults to loopback because nginx terminates TLS in front of it.
# MCP_TRUSTED_PROXIES must list the proxy's address, or X-Forwarded-For is attacker-controlled
# and the per-IP rate limiter can be bypassed by anyone who sends the header.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MCP_PORT=7379
# MCP_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1,::1
